{"step_index":91,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:47:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:47:35+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:47:35+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/sandbox.sh`\nTotal Lines: 84\nTotal Bytes: 3776\nShowing lines 1 to 84\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/bin/bash\n2: # sandbox.sh — run a command in a bubblewrap sandbox that contains only what an\n3: # Antigravity attempt needs.\n4: #\n5: #   sandbox.sh --ws DIR --home DIR --part PARTITION [--ro PATH]... -- CMD [ARGS...]\n6: #\n7: # Why this exists: agy's permission rules confine its shell commands but not its\n8: # file tools. The permission probe (job 84813) had agents write, edit and read\n9: # outside the workspace under every rule form, with no permission check logged.\n10: # So the boundary has to be the filesystem the agents can see, and this script\n11: # builds it:\n12: #\n13: #   writable   the workspace (--ws) and the private agy home (--home)\n14: #   read-only  /usr /etc and the libc trees; agy; the Lean toolchain and\n15: #              lean_project (a stray `lake` cannot delete Mathlib); the checker,\n16: #              its Python venv and code; this partition's challenges\n17: #   absent     everything else — the rest of $HOME (~/.ssh, the real OAuth token,\n18: #              other projects), the repository's results and handoff trees, and\n19: #              /run, which is where the munge socket lives: without it nothing in\n20: #              here can submit SLURM jobs\n21: #\n22: # agy's own policy file inside --home stays writable: agy rewrites it atomically\n23: # at startup, and a read-only mount on top broke that (probe 84823). It is only a\n24: # second layer — an agent that widened agy's rules would still be confined to\n25: # this filesystem. The real agy config directory is not mounted at all: the\n26: # private home carries its own copi\n<truncated 561 bytes>\n0:     --ro)   p=\"$(readlink -f \"$2\")\"; EXTRA+=(--ro-bind \"$p\" \"$p\"); shift 2 ;;\n41:     --)     shift; break ;;\n42:     *) echo \"sandbox.sh: unknown argument $1\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n43:   esac\n44: done\n45: if [ -z \"$WS\" ] || [ -z \"$HOMEDIR\" ] || [ -z \"$PART\" ] || [ $# -eq 0 ]; then\n46:   echo \"usage: sandbox.sh --ws DIR --home DIR --part PARTITION [--ro PATH]... -- CMD\" >&2; exit 2\n47: fi\n48: [ -d \"$WS\" ] && [ -d \"$HOMEDIR\" ] || { echo \"sandbox.sh: --ws and --home must exist\" >&2; exit 2; }\n49: case \"$WS/\" in\n50:   \"$ROOT/lean_project/\"*|\"$ROOT/tools/\"*|\"$ROOT/.venv/\"*|\"$ELAN/\"*|\"$CFG/\"*)\n51:     echo \"sandbox.sh: refusing a workspace inside a protected tree\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n52: esac\n53: \n54: SYS=(--ro-bind /usr /usr --ro-bind /etc /etc)\n55: for d in /bin /sbin /lib /lib64; do\n56:   if [ -L \"$d\" ]; then SYS+=(--symlink \"$(readlink \"$d\")\" \"$d\")\n57:   elif [ -d \"$d\" ]; then SYS+=(--ro-bind \"$d\" \"$d\"); fi\n58: done\n59: \n60: exec bwrap \\\n61:   --die-with-parent --new-session \\\n62:   --unshare-pid --unshare-ipc --unshare-uts --unshare-cgroup-try \\\n63:   \"${SYS[@]}\" \\\n64:   --proc /proc --dev /dev \\\n65:   --tmpfs /tmp --tmpfs /var/tmp --tmpfs /run \\\n66:   --ro-bind \"$AGY\" \"$AGY\" \\\n67:   --ro-bind \"$ELAN\" \"$ELAN\" \\\n68:   --ro-bind \"$ROOT/lean_project\" \"$ROOT/lean_project\" \\\n69:   --ro-bind \"$ROOT/.venv\" \"$ROOT/.venv\" \\\n70:   --ro-bind \"$ROOT/tools\" \"$ROOT/tools\" \\\n71:   --ro-bind \"$ROOT/pipeline\" \"$ROOT/pipeline\" \\\n72:   --ro-bind \"$ROOT/config.py\" \"$ROOT/config.py\" \\\n73:   --ro-bind \"$ROOT/benchmark/challenges_$PART\" \"$ROOT/benchmark/challenges_$PART\" \\\n74:   --ro-bind \"$ENVF\" \"$ENVF\" \\\n75:   --ro-bind \"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_lean_pat