{"step_index":145,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:50:57Z","thinking":"**Reasoning about graph walk induction**\n\nConsider induction on graph walks to demonstrate membership within a bounded ball. The base case, a nil walk, establishes that the start node equals the end node and thus lies within the ball of radius 0. For the inductive step, examine a walk constructed from an adjacency and a shorter walk.\n\nAssuming the induction hypothesis for the shorter walk, the intermediate node lies within a smaller ball. The symmetry of the adjacency then establishes that the start node of the original walk is within a ball one unit larger, leveraging a relevant lemma about the successor function within `mem_ballWithin`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Add walk to ballWithin connection lemmas\"","EndLine":"32","Instruction":"\"Add mem_ballWithin_of_walk lemmas\"","ReplacementContent":"\"lemma mem_ballWithin_succ_o